@startuml d8-routing-failover
title Choosing the node for a key, and failover (drawn from the 2.17.0 code)
participant "TcpClientCache" as tcc
participant "ReliableChannel" as rc
participant "ClientCacheAffinityContext" as aff
participant "Channel of the\nkey's primary node" as nch
participant "Fallback channel\n(see the note)" as dch
participant "ClientRetryPolicy\n(default: retry all)" as pol
participant "Server node" as srv
tcc -> rc : affinityService(cacheId, key, ...)
rc -> aff : affinityUpdateRequired(cacheId)?
alt no current mapping for the cache (missing, or older than the last topology)
  alt a last topology is known
    rc -> srv : CACHE_PARTITIONS 1101\n(one thread at a time; others go without the map)
    srv --> rc : per node: primary partitions;\nonly PARTITIONED + rendezvous caches
    rc -> aff : readPartitionsUpdateResponse
  else no last topology yet
    rc -> rc : nothing fetched;\nthe call goes without the map
  end
end
rc -> aff : affinityNode(cacheId, key)
aff --> rc : binary key -> partition ->\nprimary node id (or none)
rc -> nch : service via nodeChannels[node id]
alt connection error on the node channel (synchronous call)
  rc -> rc : onChannelFailure: close channel,\nfail listeners, roll the default
  alt one attempt is the limit
    rc -> tcc : throw the failure\n(the policy is not asked)
  else more attempts allowed
    rc -> pol : shouldRetry? (system ops: always)
    rc -> dch : applyOnDefaultChannel\n(only if the policy agrees)
    loop until success, attempts used up, or the policy says no
      dch --> rc : ClientConnectionException
      rc -> rc : onChannelFailure, next holder;\nno channel open and failures = attempts\n(the extra attempt not counted):\nreset discovery, channelsInit
      rc -> pol : shouldRetry?
    end
    rc -> tcc : throw the first failure,\nthe others suppressed
  end
end
note over dch
  first try: a random open channel if partition awareness is on, more than
  one channel is open and nothing has failed yet; otherwise the current default
  holder, which moves on when it fails.
  attempts = holders, or retryLimit if smaller and above 0;
  one more with partition awareness and more than one open channel
end note
@enduml
